loopcatcher (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a managed capture mode to the Spotify profile ("Manage Spotify",
    on by default): loopcatcher now detects a native, Flatpak or Snap
    Spotify install, launches it already routed into the capture sink,
    plays the track/album/playlist link you paste via MPRIS OpenUri, and
    closes it again when the session ends. Set "Manage Spotify" to no
    under Profile -> Profile Settings to keep the previous flow of
    opening and cueing Spotify yourself.
  * Make the Spotify profile the one a fresh install starts on, via an
    optional DEFAULT marker file inside a profile's own directory - the
    main script still names no module anywhere.
  * Enable every installed profile on a fresh config, so Change Profile
    is usable without visiting Settings first.
  * Show Player Profile first in the Welcome screen's configuration
    summary.
  * Fix a config whose enabled_profiles no longer listed its own
    default_profile silently switching to a different module instead of
    keeping - and re-enabling - the configured one.
  * Fix Ctrl+C on the Recording screen not actually stopping the capture
    - it only made the spinner disappear, leaving the track recording in
    the background.
  * Fix metadata occasionally missing from the first track of a session,
    caused by the player's MPRIS fields arriving out of order.
  * Fix the managed mode's "Spotify is already running" exit path closing
    the user's own Spotify instance on the way out.
  * Make profile teardown verify and escalate (SIGTERM to SIGKILL,
    flatpak kill to pkill), since GUI applications commonly ignore a
    plain terminating signal.
  * Narrow the default layout from 100 to 80 columns so it fits a
    standard terminal window, with every width now sized relative to the
    active language's text instead of a fixed number - the Spanish UI no
    longer overflows the box.
  * Simplify the Recording screen to what's actually useful mid-session:
    output folder, session name, capture status and a track/artist/album
    table - dropped the Config File, Audio Sink, Output File, Track No.,
    Disc No., Playback Status and Install Type rows. Progress is now
    shown by a lightweight "Catching..." spinner instead of a background
    process.
  * Make output folder and file names portable to other operating
    systems: components are now capped at 100 characters and 200 bytes
    (cut on a word boundary), never end in a dot or space, and never
    collide with a Windows device name such as CON or NUL. Long album
    titles previously produced folders Linux accepted but Windows,
    macOS and FAT/exFAT volumes rejected.

 -- Kike Fonseca <filipok@gmail.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

loopcatcher (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add English/Spanish translations for the whole app (Settings ->
    Advanced -> Language, auto-detected on first run).
  * Reduce the CLI to --help/--version/--debug/--logname - output
    directory, session name, codec, bitrate and filename scheme are now
    config/TUI-only (Settings, Session Name screen).
  * Settings/Profile Settings edits still save to disk immediately, but no
    longer reload into the running process - use the new Restart item on
    the Welcome menu to apply them.
  * Fix Ctrl+C on the Recording screen silently exiting without showing
    the Finish screen.

 -- Kike Fonseca <filipok@gmail.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0000

loopcatcher (0.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split the Spotify-specific logic out into a loadable profile module
    (profiles/spotify_native), the first step of a modular, multi-player
    architecture - the fixed Welcome/Settings/Session Name/Finish screens
    and the encoding engine now stay in the main script regardless of
    which profile is active.
  * Add a Profile menu (Change Profile / Profile Settings / About Profile)
    and an Enabled Profiles setting to the Welcome screen.
  * Rename the log_directory config key to log_file_path (now a full file
    path instead of a directory).
  * Drop the "custom" MPRIS player profile for this release - a dedicated
    generic-MPRIS module is planned for a future release.

 -- Kike Fonseca <filipok@gmail.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

